---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Procurement Signal is and who it's for.">
  <div class="page narrow">
    <div class="page-head"><h1>Procurement news, with the signal turned up.</h1></div>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>{SITE.name} is an independent publication for procurement and sourcing leaders: CPOs, category managers, sourcing leads and the teams who support them.</p>
      <p>Procurement news is scattered across trade publications, government notices, commodity markets, press wires and analyst blogs. We track all of it, connect the dots across sources, and publish our own reporting and analysis on what matters with a clear answer to the question every procurement team asks: <em>what does this mean for me?</em></p>
      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>News</strong>: significant developments, synthesized from multiple sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Procurement briefings</strong>: signal reports rated by urgency, with what changed and the first action to take.</li>
        <li><strong>Analysis</strong>: weekly trend pieces on where the function is heading.</li>
        <li><strong>Category outlook</strong>: our read on negotiating leverage, supply risk and the move to make in 12 purchase categories, with a deep dive on each.</li>
        <li><strong>Tariff and trade deadline tracker</strong>: every date that changes landed cost, with a countdown to the next one.</li>
        <li><strong>Software rankings</strong>: procurement software compared by our analysts and by G2 ratings. No vendor pays to be listed or ranked.</li>
        <li><strong>Price trends by category</strong>: monthly price-pressure readings for 12 purchase categories, built from official producer price data.</li>
        <li><strong>Guides and glossary</strong>: in-depth reference guides and plain-English definitions for procurement and supply chain professionals.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>Our newsroom uses AI-assisted research and drafting under published <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a>. Every story cites and links its original sources, and our own calculations and assessments are labeled as ours. Editor: {SITE.editor}.</p>
      <p>{SITE.name} is a personal, independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or written on behalf of any employer or procurement vendor.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
